# This file names no code owner, on purpose (#5044 step 2).
#
# The pipeline lane (docs/lane-ownership.json: "the pipeline", owner `ceo`, over `.github/workflows/`) used to
# be read here as `/.github/workflows/ @a11ign-ai-leads`, so a PR touching a workflow requested review from
# the user account behind ceo's seat. It no longer does, for two reasons:
#
# - A code-owner review cannot be met by an App (a11ign#4981), and the chairman's direction on #5044 is that
#   a11ign keeps no more free machine accounts than GitHub's terms allow -- Apps are not accounts.
# - The guard that stands in its place is the org's own owned-path check, which is the chairman's direction on
#   #5044. Note it is NOT the `ownedPaths` CI job: that one reads docs/owned-path-facts.json, which lists no
#   `.github/workflows/` path. The lane data (docs/lane-ownership.json) is kept and still derives a pipeline
#   row's `lane:<owner>` label.
#
# `require_code_owner_review` is false on the `merge-queue-main` ruleset, so nothing merges or waits on an
# entry here. An entry added back would request a review that nobody holding an App could give.
